					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6202042#post-3843681</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6202042/scp-1948-j#post-3843681</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 20 Jun 2018 22:00:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrDromeus</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3785128</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I’m just gonna be honest: I saw this and downvoted instinctively. But now I get it. It’s perfect. Beautiful. The absurdist overtones matching the surreal flavor. The alternative approach mingling with the simplistic appeal. The character comedy that we as the viewer are forced to create for ourselves, forging a multitude of unique interpretations perfect for each individual. The familiarity with animal humor draws into a deep part of our collective youth, and pulls out a nostalgic, yet fresh article for us to enjoy. We are brought further into familiarity with such colloquialisms as “ciggies” and “cold ones,” assuring as that there is no need to be afraid of harsh scientific language. Here it is safe. This horse is a character that is not only lovable, but also light-hearted and interesting as an individual. Who could resist this perfection? I myself like to imagine that even the author could not hold themselves back, adding in addendum 1948-26 as a personal comment, a trace of their true feelings. <em>Hell, I like this horse!</em> Hell, who doesn’t?</p> <p>Also lol the horse has a Russian accent isn’t that wacky.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
